# Decisions

- Treat the browser case-intake route, Zustand command ownership, PEM document-status selector, Axum upload route, AppServices processor, and restricted PostgreSQL functions as the Web-05 implementation chain.
- Publish only the approved document metadata/status relation. Keep page text, embeddings, storage identity, and parser diagnostics local.
- Use `documentSetRevision` from the authorized case read to fence uploads and later criteria/evidence work.
- Keep actual browser case-to-letter certification in Web-17. Focused component and service checks do not make that claim.
- Keep Tauri and mobile deferred until Web-17 passes.
- Retain failed diagnostics separately from qualifying evidence, including the shared-Cargo timeout, the over-broad clippy command, and the first non-qualifying sabotage attempt.
- Electric 1.8 remains in its documented automatic publication mode. A live empty-relation probe proved shape request registration in `electric_publication_default`; the product catalog supplies the exact document status relation and columns.
- Revision 6 performs a controlled local-replica cutover because the required case identifiers do not exist in revision 3 and must not be invented. It clears all synchronized rows and any checkpoint before the required columns are added; the next authorized pass refetches the complete graph.

## Adversarial repair: generation fencing

The destructive revision-6 cutover is declared with `startsNewGeneration`. The migration ledger advances to `max(stored + 1, plan)` inside the same transaction and before running cutover SQL. This preserves stale-cursor fencing when a replica generation has already advanced beyond the static plan value. A negative control observed generation remain 9; the repair advances it to 10.
